		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,4344684)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-4344684">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/spikebrennan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(908688); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=908688&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834648" alt="spikebrennan" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=908688)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/spikebrennan" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(908688); return false;" >spikebrennan</a></span> <span class="odate time_1567161836 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Aug 2019 10:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4344684">
									

<p>While I love the high concept, there are some issues:</p>
<p>Special containment procedures:</p>
<p>&quot;Historical manuals and reference books regarding the Albigensian Crusade are to be acquired and then stored in Warehouse 14-3.&quot; This is simply assembling a library.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>&quot;Existing information, online or in academia, concerning the above-mentioned event, is to be analyzed by Foundation historians and adjusted accordingly.&quot; It's not clear what &quot;adjusted accordingly&quot; means- if what you mean is that the Foundation has come up with a cover narrative of the Albigensian Crusade and wishes to alter extra-Foundation accounts, then clearly say so.</p>
<p>&quot;All historical artifacts or items found in the southern French province of Occitanie are to be assessed for anomalous properties and contained.&quot; Literally scoop up all personal property in the entire area? (And Occitanie is not a province, it's a region). I think you really mean &quot;The southern French region of Occitanie is to be surveyed for anomalous historical artifacts related to the Albigensian Crusade; any such artifacts are to be collected and contained.&quot;</p>
<p>Seems weird (but not unprecedented) for a historical period to be an SCP subject as opposed to a tangible artifact relating to that period being the SCP.</p>
<p>The old-timey grammar in &quot;Sæfernmúða Edlæcan #12 Log Transcript&quot; is cute but contains numerous distracting errors- here’s a non-exhaustive list of a few that jumped out at me:</p>
<ul>
<li>&quot;Hast&quot; is the second person singular present tense of the verb &quot;to have.&quot; &quot;Hath&quot; is the third person singular. You use them wrong. (Also, this is a usage from the King James Bible/Shakespeare era, which is an understandable stylistic choice on your part since true period Middle English would be pretty impenetrable except to Chaucer scholars.)</li>
<li>Why is Raymond named a baroness? And if he's a baron rather than an actual king, he wouldn't be addressed as &quot;majesty.&quot;</li>
<li>&quot;alloweth&quot; is also third-person singular present indicative form of the verb &quot;to allow&quot;.</li>
<li>&quot;We has't hath reached&quot;. Not sure how this is supposed to be parsed.</li>
</ul>
<p>I think the article could be dramatically improved with some grammatical proofreading of the faux-historical documents. (It’s also not clear in-universe why they’d be written this way- if the Foundation has translated the documents from medieval French, why would the output be in Elizabethan English?)</p>
<p>No issue with the substantive content of the documents, though - you're telling a cool story and I like it. (I especially like your in-universe explanation for why there are so many medieval manuscript doodles of knights battling snails.)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
